00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hey dad what are you doing danny keep it  down you'll scare away the ghosts  i've always thought there was something  special about the tv show danny phantom  and i think it can be summed up in one  critical phrase self-awareness writers  butch hartman and steve marmel were  entirely aware of exactly what they  wanted to make and they made just that  danny phantom is likely one of the most  well-known kids tv shows from the  mid-2000s because of its unique ability  to improve upon well-established cliches  and tropes present in many other  cartoons the show is completely aware of  what it is a one-of-a-kind cliche-filled  serialized kids tv show but why exactly  do you remember danny phantom so well  let's take a deeper look  [Music]  watching through dany phantom you would  probably recognize a ton of tropes and  cliches that would typically bring down  an animated tv show danny phantom  however is able to bring these tropes to  life in what i would say is a better way  than we've ever seen before things such  as the cliche evil night the typical  christmas special episode crossovers  with other series the will they want  their relationship between two of the  main characters the nerdy best friend  and even the evil future self battle in  most cases danny phantom not only does  these things better than other shows but  it was the first time in their lives  that many kids had ever seen such tropes  for sure we've seen things like the evil  night trope and scooby-doo and the  others in tons of different shows but  danny phantom was able to do them in a  way that was just so memorable and i  think that comes back to the show's  creator butch hartman and his  self-awareness about what the show truly  was hartmann has created several kids tv  series including tough puppy danny  phantom and fairly oddparents he was  uniquely aware of what each of his shows  were trying to accomplish and because of  this they're some of the most popular  kids shows of all time while fairly odd  appearance had the longest run and was  likely the most popular out of his shows  i believe danny phantom is the most  memorable of all one of the show's best  episodes secret weapons which we got  near the end of the second season truly  captures the nature of why the show is  so unforgettable while there are  probably episodes which you remember  better such as the ultimate enemy where  we saw dany's evil future self or  mystery meet where we were first  introduced to the show and met the evil  lunch lady ghost the episode's secret  weapons shows us exactly why the show is  so memorable the episode begins with  team phantom coming out of the movie  theater as danny turns invisible to hide  from his sister jazz ever since she  found out about dany's ghost powers and  became the latest member of team phantom  jazz has been trying her hardest to fit  in with them but keeps failing at ghost  hunting an angry dany then drives her  away and she seeks help from the evil  vlad masters this episode gives us three  different reasons as to why the series  is so memorable its use of witty banter  serialization and striking animation  upon re-watching this particular episode  one thing really stood out to me the  banter dany is able to perfectly emulate  the ever so famous quips that spider-man  is known for when fighting the bad guys  the episode actually makes note of this  even showing how jazz is completely  incapable of making her banter as witty  as dany's when it comes to puns and  one-liners that would typically be  groan-worthy dany is able to make them  seem natural and pretty funny at times a  lot of this banter seemed to be a bit  ahead of its time for an animated series  just like its serialization serialized  television shows are ones which have a  continuing plot that unfolds in a  sequential episode by episode fashion at  the time and even still now most child  focused and animated tv shows were not  serialized meaning you could watch any  episode and not miss a beat danny  phantom on the other hand had gradual  progression throughout the series it  shows danny as he gains new powers and  grows as an individual along with his  sister his friends and even his parents  it was one of the first kids animated tv  shows to show such intimate character  growth across seasons and it even  influenced other shows on the same  network avatar the last airbender is  probably one of the greatest displays of  character growth in an animated kids  series and it might not have been  possible without the serialization of  danny phantom the serialized nature of  both avatar and danny phantom truly  helped them to stand apart from the  other shows on nick at the time such as  spongebob jimmy neutron and hey arnold  one of the biggest things that set danny  phantom apart from the rest though was  its striking animation if i had to say  the one thing i remember the most about  danny phantom it would be the unique  character designs and color usage given  to us by butch hartman he made such  striking animation throughout every  episode that it really sticks in the  mind of anyone who watches the show the  theme song in particular had one of the  most remarkable animation and music  sequences of any intro theme song of the  time it's really this stunning animation  and character design that started the  fandom for the show and led to the  creation of butch hartman's best series  and i believe the show is hartman's best  because it grew with its fans his other  shows were made more for kids and for  the most part they stayed that way but  as fans matured danny phantom and his  characters matured as well offering  something new each season that's why the  fandom is still as strong as ever with  fans constantly asking for a reboot of  the series the impact danny phantom had  on the animation industry can't really  ever be quantified it tested the limits  of animation storytelling and allowed  for future shows to push the boundaries  even further hartman created something  that fans will always want to come back  to which is exactly why danny phantom is  so unforgettable and why it will never  go ghost anyways that's gonna be all for  today if you like what you saw maybe  check out the video on your screen for  some different content i make videos on  basically anything that interests me in  the world of entertainment also don't  forget to like and subscribe as it truly  does help me out and thanks for watching  rocket riley  you

